Imported trees
--------------

doc/provenance.md lists every imported directory with its upstream
repository and the revision it was taken at.
In summary:

  * core/ and applications/* imported from the 2600Hz kazoo-* repositories:
    Mozilla Public License 2.0, as published by 2600Hz.

  * configs/freeswitch and configs/kamailio, from 2600Hz's
    kazoo-configs-freeswitch and kazoo-configs-kamailio repositories. These
    repositories carry no license file; their RPM packaging declares them as
    Mozilla Public License 1.1.

  * vendor/amqp_dist, from 2600Hz's erlang-amqp_dist. The upstream
    repository carries no license file and its source files no license
    headers. vendor/amqp_dist/NOTICE records where the code came from; no
    license grant is stated for it here.


Third-party material
--------------------

  * freeswitch/mod_reprise: files ported from FreeSWITCH's mod_kazoo keep
    their original Mozilla Public License 1.1 notices (Anthony Minessale II
    and the mod_kazoo contributors). Files that carry portions of mod_kazoo
    or of Kazoo's ecallmgr say so in their headers. See
    freeswitch/mod_reprise/README.md, section "License".

  * docker/freeswitch/patches: patches to FreeSWITCH, applied when the
    FreeSWITCH image is built. See docker/freeswitch/patches/README.md.

Third-party Erlang dependencies are not part of this tree; the build fetches
them into deps/ (make/deps.mk) and each carries its own license.


Container images
----------------

The container images built from this tree (docker/) also contain software
that is not part of this repository, under its own licenses: among others
Erlang/OTP, FreeSWITCH, Kamailio, Monster UI and its applications, nginx,
the Kazoo sounds, and the Debian packages each image installs. Their
licenses are those of the respective projects.


